# Match Fit product copy

## Do not market with heavy AI language

Match Fit uses algorithms and structured signals for discovery and matching. **Do not** position the product as an "AI platform" or "AI-powered matching" in user-facing marketing, legal summaries, onboarding, or homepage copy.

| Prefer | Avoid (user-facing) |
|--------|---------------------|
| algorithmic matching | AI matching, AI-assisted matching, AI-powered matching |
| algorithmic surfacing / ranking | AI learns how you behave |
| match profile / discovery profile | AI match profile |
| structured questionnaire signals | AI suggests coaches |

**OK to keep "AI"** only for internal admin tools (AI Assistant, Outreach HQ generation, content calendar generation, optional listing price check) — label them as operator tools, not core product marketing.

Internal code names (`aiMatchProfileText`, etc.) may stay; do not surface those names to users.

## Fitness Pro vs trainer

**Fitness Pro** / **Fitness Pros** — canonical label for all non-client professionals on the platform (personal trainers, coaches, nutritionists, specialists).

| Use **Fitness Pro(s)** | Keep **trainer** |
|------------------------|------------------|
| Marketplace, signup, waitlist, admin metrics | Assigned coach in a session ("your trainer" in PT/DIY copy) |
| Directory, discovery, Fit Hub author role | Personal training industry positioning |
| Legal defined term for platform professionals | Service types: "personal training", CPT, "Certified Personal Trainer" badge |
| Sign-up CTAs, counters, featured listings | Code routes (`/trainer/`), API fields, DB columns |

**Trainer Dashboard** → **Fitness Pro Dashboard** in user-facing nav when referring to the pro portal product.

When editing Terms or Privacy, update the defined **Fitness Pro** term consistently; coordinate section headings with legal meaning.
